 compression and system co-design for efficient\n  long context inference}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Findings of ACL 2025}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Shutova et~al.(2025)Shutova, Malinovskii, Egiazarian, Kuznedelev,\n  Mazur, Surkov, Ermakov, and Alistarh}]{shutova2025aquakv}\nAlina Shutova, Vladimir Malinovskii, Vage Egiazarian, Denis Kuznedelev, Denis\n  Mazur, Nikita Surkov, Ivan Ermakov, and Dan Alistarh. 2025.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.19392} {Cache me if you must:\n  Adaptive key-value quantization for large language models}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{ICML 2025}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Su et~al.(2025)Su, Chen, Shen, Wei, Li, Yu, and\n  Yuan}]{su2025rotatekv}\nZunhai Su, Zhe Chen, Wang Shen, Hanyu Wei, Linge Li, Huangqi Yu, and Kehong\n  Yuan. 2025.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2501.16383} {{RotateKV}: Accurate and\n  robust 2-bit {KV} cache quantization for {LLMs} via outlier-aware adaptive\n  rotations}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{IJCAI 2025}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Voita et~al.(2019)Voita, Talbot, Moiseev, Sennrich, and\n  Titov}]{voita2019analyzing}\nElena Voita, David Talbot, Fedor Moiseev, Rico Sennrich, and Ivan Titov. 2019.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/1905.09418} {Analyzing multi-head\n  self-attention: Specialized heads do the heavy lifting, the rest can be\n  pruned}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{ACL 2019}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Wang et~al.(2019)Wang, Liu, Lin, Lin, and Han}]{wang2019haq}\nKuan Wang, Zhijian Liu, Yujun Lin, Ji~Lin, and Song Han. 2019.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/1811.08886} {{HAQ}: Hardware-aware\n  automated quantization with mixed precision}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{CVPR 2019}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Xia et~al.(2025)Xia, Wu, Li, Wu, Wang, Wang, Li, Singhal, Shah,\n  Ariyak, Zhuang, Zhou, Athiwaratkun, Zheng, and Song}]{xia2025kitty}\nHaojun Xia, Xiaoxia Wu, Jisen Li, Robert Wu, Junxiong Wang, Jue Wang, Chenxi\n  Li, Aman Singhal, Alay~Dilipbhai Shah, Alpay Ariyak, Donglin Zhuang, Zhongzhu\n  Zhou, Ben Athiwaratkun, Zhen Zheng, and Shuaiwen~Leon Song. 2025.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2511.18643} {{Kitty}: Accurate and\n  efficient 2-bit {KV} cache quantization with dynamic channel-wise precision\n  boost}.\n\\newblock \\emph{Preprint}, arXiv:2511.18643.\n\\newblock ArXiv preprint.\n\n\\bibitem[{Xiao et~al.(2024)Xiao, Tian, Chen, Han, and\n  Lewis}]{xiao2024streamingllm}\nGuangxuan Xiao, Yuandong Tian, Beidi Chen, Song Han, and Mike Lewis. 2024.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2309.17453} {Efficient streaming\n  language models with attention sinks}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{ICLR 2024}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Yang et~al.(2024)Yang, Han, Gao, Hu, Zhang, and\n  Zhao}]{yang2024pyramidinfer}\nDongjie Yang, Xiaodong Han, Yan Gao, Yao Hu, Shilin Zhang, and Hai Zhao. 2024.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.12532} {{PyramidInfer}: Pyramid\n  {KV} cache compression for high-throughput {LLM} inference}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{Findings of ACL 2024}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Zhang et~al.(2025)Zhang, Zeng, Peng, Zhuang, and\n  Chen}]{zhang2025mixkvq}\nTao Zhang, Ziqian Zeng, Hao Peng, Huiping Zhuang, and Cen Chen. 2025.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.19206} {{MixKVQ}: Query-aware\n  mixed-precision {KV} cache quantization for long-context reasoning}.\n\\newblock \\emph{Preprint}, arXiv:2512.19206.\n\\newblock ArXiv preprint.\n\n\\bibitem[{Zhang et~al.(2023)Zhang, Sheng, Zhou, Chen, Zheng, Cai, Song, Tian,\n  R{\\'{e}}, Barrett, Wang, and Chen}]{zhang2023h2o}\nZhenyu Zhang, Ying Sheng, Tianyi Zhou, Tianlong Chen, Lianmin Zheng, Ruisi Cai,\n  Zhao Song, Yuandong Tian, Christopher R{\\'{e}}, Clark Barrett, Zhangyang\n  Wang, and Beidi Chen. 2023.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.14048} {{H2O}: Heavy-hitter oracle\n  for efficient generative inference of large language models}.\n\\newblock In \\emph{NeurIPS 2023}.\n\n\\bibitem[{Zuo et~al.(2026)Zuo, Zhou, Cong, Xi, and Leung}]{zuo2026ratequant}\nFei Zuo, Zikang Zhou, Hao Cong, Xiaoyan Xi, and Ho~Fai Leung. 2026.\n\\newblock \\href {https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.06675} {{RateQuant}: Optimal\n  mixed-precision {KV} cache quantization via rate-distortion theory}.\n\\newblock \\emph{Preprint}, arXiv:2605.06675.\n\\newblock ArXiv preprint.\n\n\\end{thebibliography}\n","numLines":252,"startLine":1,"totalLines":252}}}
